    "obs_and_metrics": [],
    "innovation": "This paper uses integrated assessment modeling to demonstrate that achieving the 2\u00b0C climate target without immediate, drastic cuts is critically dependent on the large-scale, yet highly uncertain, future availability of negative emission technologies like bio-energy with carbon capture and storage (BECCS).",
    "kg_extraction_triplets": [
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "IMAGE",
            "source_entity_type": "Source",
            "relation": "HAS_SOURCE_COMPONENT",
            "target_entity_instance": "MAGICC6",
            "target_entity_type": "SourceComponent",
            "paragraph": "In order to explore the potential for BECCS further, we have run a set of alternative climate policy scenarios: i.e. stabilization cases at 2.6 and 2.9 W/m\u00b2 (450 and 480 ppm CO2-eq.) using the IMAGE model with and without BECCS (IMAGE can directly be run under radiative forcing targets, and thus does not need cumulative emission targets). The IMAGE model provides a description of various systems relevant for global environmental change (Bouwman et al. 2006). The climate system is represented by parts of the MAGICC6 model, while the carbon cycle is represented by a detailed description of the interaction between the biosphere, oceans and the atmosphere.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        }
